// =====================================================================
// Yokai Descent - an anime-flavored action roguelike, written in Volt.
//
// Fight down through four haunted floors. Every floor is five rooms:
// three fights, a shop and a boss. Rooms are generated fresh each run,
// you pick a blessing card after every fight, and when you fall the run
// is gone (permadeath) - but the spirit shards you earned buy permanent
// upgrades at the Shrine on the title screen.
//
// Art credits: the three heroes and the ninja enemies are from CraftPix's free
// yokai, ninja and magic-effects sprite packs (see craftpix.net/file-licenses), the
// UI panels are drawn by art/build_ui2.py, the other enemies, bosses and tiles are drawn by
// art/build_hi.py, and sound effects and slash effects are the CC0 files Moonwell uses.
//
// Controls
//   Move          WASD or arrow keys
//   Slash         Z or Space  (hold to keep swinging, it also parries shots)
//   Spirit bolt   X           (uses a charge, charges slowly refill)
//   Dash          C or Shift  (you can't be hit while dashing)
//   Menus         arrows + Z, number keys 1-3 pick cards
//   Pause         P or Esc    (shows the blessings you hold)
//   Music         M
// On phones: stick + slash, bolt and dash buttons.
// =====================================================================
#html

title "Yokai Descent"
canvas 320, 180
// hi-res: the screen is 640x360 real pixels but the game still thinks in 320x180,
// so detailed sprites can be drawn at scale 50 (one picture pixel = one screen pixel)
# __cv.width = 640; __cv.height = 360; __cx = __cv.getContext('2d'); __cx.imageSmoothingEnabled = false; __cx.scale(2, 2);
touchpad "z", "x", "c" stick "../dungeon/controls/stick.png", "../dungeon/controls/nub.png" button "../dungeon/controls/button.png" icons "../dungeon/controls/sword.png", "../dungeon/controls/summon.png", "../dungeon/controls/dash.png"

